WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.020
What’s the difference between a migrant
and refugee?

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.380
“Migrant” is an umbrella term for asylum
seekers, refugees, and economic migrants.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.140
Asylum seekers are people fleeing persecution
or conflict.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.020
Once an asylum claim is approved, the asylum
seeker becomes a refugee.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:22.380
The UN will sometimes give people from countries
like Syria blanket refugee status.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:28.000
Refugees are entitled to rights and protections spelled
out in international treaties.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.360
Economic migrants are people who leave home
to look for work.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.380
They are not entitled to the same protections
as refugees under international law.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.020
In reality, these two groups can and often
overlap.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.540
Many people fleeing conflict are often looking
to escape poverty, too.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.980
This is an important distinction to make when
responding to crises.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.680
Like those unfolding around the world today.

